                <p rendition="#flush">I <hi rendition="#italic">Hearing of the Yugoslav and Italian
                        Representatives</hi></p>
                <p>It was <hi rendition="#italic">agreed</hi>, on the proposal of the Chairman, that
                    the representatives of Yugoslavia and Italy should be admitted to the Council to
                    express their views on Article 16 and that the Yugoslav representative should be
                    heard first.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">M. Simić</hi>, Foreign Minister of Yugoslavia, read a
                    statement in English and submitted a proposal concerning Article 16 of the Draft
                    Peace Treaty (see doc. CFM (46) (NY)
                        5),<anchor n="63" xml:id="d306-f1"/> together with a map of a new line
                    proposed for the frontier between Yugoslavia and Italy.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">M. Tarchiani</hi>, Ambassador of Italy to Washington,
                    read a statement in English (see doc. CFM (46)
                        (NY) 6).<anchor n="64" xml:id="d306-f2"/></p>
                <pb facs="1055" n="1031" xml:id="pg1031"/>
                <p>The Representatives of Yugoslavia and Italy then left the Council Room.</p>
                <p>It was <hi rendition="#italic">agreed</hi> that the statements made by the
                    Yugoslav and Italian Representatives and the new Yugoslav proposals for Article
                    16 of the Italian Treaty would be examined by the Council when it considered for
                    a second time the Paris Conference recommendation on that Article. It would then
                    be open also to any member of the Council to move an amendment to the Council’s
                    previous decision on the frontier line.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">II <hi rendition="#italic">Recommendations of the Paris
                        Conference on the Peace Treaty With Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Continuation of First Reading</hi>)<anchor n="65" xml:id="d306-f3"/></p>
                <p>The Council resumed its consideration of the unagreed Articles with the following
                    results:</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Annex III. Ceded Territories</hi></p>
                <p>Consideration <hi rendition="#italic">deferred</hi> as no recommendation received
                    from the Paris Conference.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Annex VI. Part B, Insurance</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Referred to the Deputies</hi> for further study.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Annex VII. Part III, Negotiable Instruments</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Adopted</hi>.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Annex VII. Part V, U.S. Proposal</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Reserved</hi> for further study.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Annex VIII. Judgments</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Adopted</hi>.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">III <hi rendition="#italic">Next Meeting of the
                    Council</hi></p>
                <p>Friday, November 8, at 3:30 p.m.</p>
                <p>Agenda: Review of points still outstanding in the Peace Treaty with Italy.</p>
